{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788809597454403001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"chippable-potty-dipper","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"62c505110d128bdf9490f2fc5e15831d8cfafb88ccb38545d28ba9220245b5f8","event_uuid":"27cb27f1-6dda-4680-9ec5-a58538626897","position":{"commit_sha":"25bb631f4a725bf0ab73a8e35721a7a3f63a66a0","position":"1788807433542832004-27cb27f1-6dda-4680-9ec5-a58538626897"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c1a4daf150ec6c3e69c14dd41490aa6cd6395109d259f26e1e0917af15e496a9","event_uuid":"4ba11b4d-55af-493c-8e3b-95086a0e46bf","position":{"commit_sha":"dbadb8d6a2a05969f8c2fb746e6e47649ebe8df6","position":"1788807561385885128-4ba11b4d-55af-493c-8e3b-95086a0e46bf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a3b64e287c91cd55c1aa2a68ab6853a727ca16ac93eab9561822689457dc66fb","event_uuid":"02074659-23f1-46e6-bd94-6fad4122ec21","position":{"commit_sha":"d54c5f7725fb8d3b61465c0a71de40ec75ba77c5","position":"1788807608480193144-02074659-23f1-46e6-bd94-6fad4122ec21"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788807433542832004,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"02074659-23f1-46e6-bd94-6fad4122ec21","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"f75f-5d85-7b9a-4d86"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`run_bridge` spawns `rebar bridge sync|preview` (`MODE_COMMANDS`, `_bridge_runner.py:26-31`), which spawns the engine via `subprocess.call` with no timeout (`_cli/_bridge_commands.py:51`, `launch_reconciler`, `engine_env`): the hop chain is `_bridge_runner._run(MODE_COMMANDS[profile])` (`:112-123,216`) → `rebar bridge sync` → `launch_reconciler` → `python -m rebar_reconciler sync`. On the 3600 s timeout the runner kills only the middle process; the engine grandchild is orphaned (PPID 1) holding the pass lock until lease expiry. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\n1. `MODE_COMMANDS` becomes `MODE_ARGS: Mapping[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\"dry-run\": (\"preview\",), \"bootstrap-strict\": (\"sync\",\"--max-changes\",\"10\"), \"bootstrap-throttle\": (\"sync\",\"--max-changes\",\"100\"), \"live\": (\"sync\",)}`; argv = `(sys.executable, \"-m\", \"rebar.reconciler\", *MODE_ARGS[profile], \"--repo-root\", str(root))`.\n2. Replace `_run` with `_spawn_bounded(argv, *, root, environ) -> CompletedProcess`: `Popen(..., cwd=root, env=environ, stdin=DEVNULL, stdout=PIPE, stderr=PIPE, text=True, errors=\"replace\", start_new_session=(os.name==\"posix\"))`, `communicate(timeout=TIMEOUT_SECONDS)`; on `TimeoutExpired` → `rebar._proc.reap_process_group(proc, grace=_REAP_GRACE_S=10.0, drain=_REAP_DRAIN_S=5.0, label=\"bridge\", logger=logger)` then re-raise so the existing \"timed out\" branches (`:217-219,260-270`) stay. Use it for the delivery child too (`_delivery_command` `:172-192` unchanged, credential-stripped env unchanged).\n3. SIGTERM does not run the engine's `finally`; lock recovery stays with the lease/steal path (`_pass_lock_lifecycle`); no signal handler is added. `launch_reconciler` remains the operator CLI path (`rebar bridge preview|sync`).\n4. Exit-code ownership: the engine child (`__main__._finish_disposition`, `:95-113`) is the single owner of canonicalisation for `preview`/`sync`; `_classified_result` (`:154-169`) keeps only the `BRIDGE_STATE:` marker parse for the state name and returns `(state, returncode)` with the child's exit code unchanged; the `legacy_exit` table walk (`:166-168`) is deleted because the runner now only invokes canonical routes. An exit 0 without a marker is `(\"converged\", 0)`; a non-zero exit without a marker is `(\"operational_failure\", rc)` with `rc` propagated verbatim (a child exiting 2 with no marker is `(\"operational_failure\", 2)`, never `invalid_invocation`).\n5. `docs/exit-codes.md:37-41` states: \"canonical 0/1/2 is produced once, in the engine child, for the `preview`/`sync` routes; `rebar bridge run` propagates the child's exit unchanged and reads `BRIDGE_STATE:`/`BRIDGE_PAUSED:` only for the state name; 3/4/75 survive only on the argument-less direct-engine route.\" The `docs/user-guide.md` bridge-run section describes the direct spawn.\n\nBREAKING: `rebar bridge run` no longer invokes `rebar bridge sync|preview` as a subprocess; profiles map to engine `preview`/`sync` argv directly.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py`, `docs/exit-codes.md:37-59`, `docs/user-guide.md` (bridge run section), `tests/unit/test_bridge_runner*.py` (existing runner tests that assert the `rebar bridge …` argv). Out of scope: `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py` (`launch_reconciler` stays as the operator path), the engine's own signal handling, and `rebar._proc.reap_process_group` (consumed as-is).\n\n## Testing\nHappy: runner unit tests assert argv `[sys.executable, \"-m\", \"rebar.reconciler\", \"sync\", \"--repo-root\", root]` for `live` and `--max-changes 10` for `bootstrap-strict`; `Popen` called with `start_new_session=True` on POSIX. Edge: monkeypatch `TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1` and spawn a stub `-m` target that itself spawns `sleep 30` (the grandchild) → after `run_bridge` returns `operational_failure`, `os.kill(grandchild_pid, 0)` raises `ProcessLookupError` (`python3 scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` clean); a child exiting non-zero with no marker maps to `(\"operational_failure\", rc)` with `rc` propagated verbatim; a delivery-child timeout still reaps. Commands: `pytest tests/unit/test_bridge_runner*.py -q`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `_bridge_runner.py` contains no `\"rebar\", \"bridge\"` argv and no `legacy_exit` reference — grep.\n- [ ] Timeout test proves the grandchild is reaped (no PPID-1 survivor) — `pytest tests/unit/test_bridge_runner*.py -q` plus `python3 scripts/check_orphaned_load.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/exit-codes.md` states the single owner as specified — grep for \"produced once, in the engine child\".\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py","reason":"direct engine spawn + reap"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"ownership statement"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"bridge run hop"},{"path":"tests/unit/","reason":"runner tests (tests/unit/test_bridge_runner*.py)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","f75f-5d85-7b9a-4d86"],["parent","ebf5-5d21-0124-4313"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"cfbd-97a9-ff1d-4945","ticket_type":"story","title":"Spawn python -m rebar.reconciler directly from _bridge_runner and reap the process group on timeout","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["27cb27f1-6dda-4680-9ec5-a58538626897","4ba11b4d-55af-493c-8e3b-95086a0e46bf","02074659-23f1-46e6-bd94-6fad4122ec21"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788809597454403001,"uuid":"031d6676-d501-4bb4-83f7-27ec28fd0200"}